        <activityName xml:lang="en">Methanol distillation, hydrogen from electrolysis, CO2 from MSWI (100:0 alloc.)</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Methanol distillation, hydrogen from electrolysis, CO2 from MSWI (100:0 alloc.)
Adapted from Comparative well-to-wheel life cycle assessment of OME3â€“5 synfuel production via the power-to-liquid pathway, Hank et al. 2019. Note that a 100:0 CO2 alloc. factor is applied: the carbon dioxide emissions are allocated to the MSWI plant, but the carbon capture efforts are within the system boundaries of the fuel producer. The combustion of the resulting methanol does not lead to carbon dioxide emissions. For more information, refer to Section I.C0.6 of Sacchi and Bauer, 2023. Source: Comparative well-to-wheel life cycle assessment of OME3â€“5 synfuel production via the power-to-liquid pathway. Christoph Hank, Lukas Lazar, Franz Mantei, Mohamed Ouda, Robin J. White, Tom Smolinka, Achim Schaadt, Christopher Hebling and Hans-Martin Henning. 2019. https://doi.org/10.1039/C9SE00658C

